# NOTE: knowledge_base/chroma_db/ is intentionally NOT ignored — the prebuilt
# index (~15 MB) ships in git so an air-gapped beamline machine has a working RAG
# on checkout with no re-index step. (.DS_Store inside it is still caught by the
# global macOS rule above.) Re-emit + recommit after changing any source doc:
#   uv run python knowledge_base/index_knowledge.py

# Knowledge Base - Keep tracked files
!knowledge_base/data/*.json
!knowledge_base/*.py
!knowledge_base/README.md

# Knowledge Base - ship the open MIDAS reference docs (public, from the MIDAS repo)
# so the RAG KB source travels with a fresh checkout. The logbooks/*.md blanket
# ignore above still protects the drop-zone for any proprietary beamtime notes an
# operator adds. Add a line here when a new open MIDAS doc is added to the KB.
!knowledge_base/logbooks/FF_HEDM_Handbook.md
!knowledge_base/logbooks/FF_HEDM_Lab_Notebook.md
!knowledge_base/logbooks/NF_HEDM_Handbook.md
!knowledge_base/logbooks/NF_HEDM_Lab_Notebook.md
