# Benchmark suite (APEXA-Bench) IS released here alongside the framework it drives.
# Track code + task/scenario defs + reference ground truth + the safety traces that
# back the paper; exclude the multi-GB regenerable detector data and loose scratch.
benchmark/detector_zoo/ge/
benchmark/detector_zoo/pilatus/
benchmark/detector_zoo/varex_aero/
benchmark/detector_zoo/varex_distortion/
# ...but ship the GSAS-II instrument parameters (208 B each). refine_v2.py needs
# them and they cannot be derived from the released frames; the ~95 MB integrated
# patterns stay out and are regenerable via the documented calibrate+integrate path.
!benchmark/detector_zoo/*/refinement/
!benchmark/detector_zoo/*/refinement/instrument.instprm
benchmark/results/day2/
benchmark/results/smoke_*/
benchmark/results/*.json
benchmark/results/*.log
benchmark/**/*.bak
# but DO ship the NIST reference structure (overrides the generic CeO2_*.cif rule)
!benchmark/detector_zoo/CeO2_NIST_5p41165.cif

# Internal release admin paperwork (Argonne Inventor Portal disclosures,
